From 96f9bcd4dcce172139e334c6e8f54c53f69ef6fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pugant <pugant@local>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 09:56:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] graph: clear t_h_pre_norm in llm_graph_result::reset()
 (root-cause fix from PR #90)

Absorbed from external PR #90 commit bc158b88c (the only hunk of that
commit that applies to this tree). llm_graph_result::reset() cleared
every other output tensor pointer but left t_h_pre_norm pointing at the
previous graph's tensor, so a graph that does not produce pre-norm
output (e.g. the DFlash decoder KV-injection path) left a stale pointer
that the post-decode extraction dereferenced (backend == nullptr
asserts, random-tensor aliasing).

Our dflash.cpp call-site clears (commit ebf1cc855) remain as harmless
belt-and-suspenders; this makes the invariant hold for every arch.

PR #90 reconciliation (branch t8-ngram): the rest of the PR is a
separate DFlash2 port variant superseded by our ba2485545 + ebf1cc855
porting already in main - see the task report for the file matrix.

Co-Authored-By: Thomas <mail@serrynaimo.com>
Co-Authored-By: GLM by z.ai <glm@z.ai>
---
 src/llama-graph.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/llama-graph.cpp b/src/llama-graph.cpp
index 4fd8ef776..f98301ab1 100644
--- a/src/llama-graph.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-graph.cpp
@@ -1002,6 +1002,7 @@ void llm_graph_result::reset() {
     t_logits      = nullptr;
     t_embd        = nullptr;
     t_embd_pooled = nullptr;
+    t_h_pre_norm  = nullptr; // was never reset: stale pointers alias random tensors when a graph does not produce it
 
     t_layer_inp.resize(LLAMA_MAX_LAYERS + 1);
     std::fill(t_layer_inp.begin(), t_layer_inp.end(), nullptr);
